<p>Definitely creepy, with a nice modern-Lovecraftian vibe. I'm normally one to be bored by slow starts, and I disagree with Yoric about the first few paragraphs. It introduces the character nicely, sets up the "everyman" feel, and establishes a starting point of profound normalcy, from which the story gradually departs. And now, my anal-retentive son-of-a-teacher side presents:</p>
<p>*Enter the Nitpicker*<br />
The second sentence of the first paragraph is a bit awkward. For one thing, the "that" near the end needs to go, and I'd consider replacing the commas with parentheses or rearranging a bit.</p>
<p>Twelfth paragraph, sixth and seventh sentences feel awkward. No idea what to do about it though.</p>
<p><em>Edit:</em> Minor fixes complete.</p>

